 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A good predictor is right most of the time. To profit, the machine must act on its guesses: fetch, issue and even execute instructions beyond a branch before the branch is decided. That is speculation, and it needs one more structure."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Hardware speculation and the reorder buffer"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here are the eight stages."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why speculate, the reorder buffer, the four steps, and our example with a commit column."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Then a snapshot, a mispredicted branch, precise exceptions and stores, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[4..=7]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: to speculate is to execute instructions past a predicted branch, before knowing whether the prediction is right."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 8: why speculate"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The danger: if the guess was wrong, those instructions must leave no trace. Not in the registers, not in memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And exceptions must be precise: if an instruction faults, every earlier instruction has finished and no later one has changed anything. Plain Tomasulo cannot promise that, since it writes registers out of order."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The fix: let instructions finish out of order, but make their results official in program order. That final step is called commit."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "execute out of order · commit in order"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rob",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: the reorder buffer, or ROB, holds every instruction between issue and commit. Each entry has four fields."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 8: the reorder buffer"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "rob"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The instruction type: a branch, a store, or an operation that writes a register."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "rob[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The destination: the register number, or for a store, the memory address."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "rob[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The value, once computed, and a ready flag."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "rob[2..=3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "What changes from Tomasulo? Results go into the ROB, not the register file. The registers hold only committed values."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "rob"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "robx"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "robx[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Tags are now ROB entry numbers. A waiting instruction can take its operand from a finished entry that has not yet committed. So the ROB does the renaming, and supplies values too."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "robx[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And the ROB is a circular queue: instructions enter at the tail in program order and leave from the head in the same order."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "robx[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "the ROB: results wait here until they commit"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "steps",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: now there are four steps."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 8: four steps"
